WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.310
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.280
T-T-That’s...!

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.440
It’s a Leaf Stone!

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.530
Thank you, Wanpachi!

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.460
You fetched it?

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.420
I’ll use this to evolve Tamatama!

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:41.720
That sounds great!

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:43.980
All right...

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.910
Yeah!

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.360
Nasshi’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.590
Nasshi! Coconut Pokémon!
Grass/Psychic type!

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:02.860
It is called “The Walking
Tropical Rainforest”!

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:06.030
Its three heads think independently!

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:09.630
However, they are friendly
and never appear to squabble!

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.990
Congratulations, Nasshi!

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.830
I’d really like you
to meet Alolan Nasshi!

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.760
Are the Alolan ones
really all that different?

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.600
Yeah! They’re like...

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.890
...<i>this</i> huge!

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.310
I hope you’ll see, interact with,
and catch loads of Alolan Pokémon!

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.290
Yeah!

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.880
Are you excited to go
back to Alola, Pikachu?

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.040
All right, Director, we’re off!

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.160
Wanpachi, look after the place
while we’re gone.

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:47.830
All right, let’s go to Alola!

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:30.940
Blue seas, blue skies
and the brightly shining sun.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.210
This is the Alola Region’s
Melemele Island,
Melemele Island, Alola Region

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:37.940
a tropical island
filled with lush nature.
Melemele Island, Alola Region

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:43.780
Satoshi!

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.580
Professor Kukui!

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.920
Oh, wait!

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.220
Alola, Professor Kukui!

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.920
Alola, Satoshi.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.250
Welcome back.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:56.790
I’m glad to be back!

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.080
You look well, Pikachu.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.590
Sheesh. You had to run off
on your own...

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.550
How was I supposed to say hi?

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.030
Sorry.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:12.890
Professor Kukui is a teacher
at the Pokémon School in Alola, and...

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.390
Hey, where’s Professor Burnet?

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:17.950
She’s waiting at home.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:18.910
I see.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:23.680
The Professors are my Alolan family,
as well as Pikachu’s.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.310
Family?

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.870
Alola, Go.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.000
A-Alola...

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.330
Aren’t those a Rabbifoot
and a Messon?!

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:37.020
It’s my first time
seeing them in person.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.910
Did you catch them in Galar, Go?

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:41.810
Yes.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.810
I bet you can pull off some strong kicks
with those legs, Rabbifoot.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.780
And Messon...

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.110
...really trusts you, Go.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:54.480
That proves you’re
taking good care of it.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.420
I’m home!

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.240
Welcome home, you two.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.460
Alola, Professor Burnet!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.370
And... Lei, was it?

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.370
That’s right...
Big brother Satoshi.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.340
Big brother...?

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.920
Nice to meet you, Lei.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.440
Your hands are tiny!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.280
No, Lei!

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:33.950
Come on in, Go.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.650
Hope I’m not a bother...

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.740
Mokuroh! Lugarugan!
Gaogaen! Melmetal!

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:50.480
I really missed you all!

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:55.290
Watch it, you’re heavy!

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:02.630
Everyone, these are my friends
Go, Rabbifoot and Messon.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.960
That’s a real Blast Burn of a welcome.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.520
Speaking of welcomes, there’s gonna be
a welcome party for you two,

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.500
so come to the Pokémon School.
Mao wanted me to tell you.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.470
All right!
I’ll make sure to be there!

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.650
Welcome party?
For me, too?

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.530
We’re off!

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.400
Have a nice trip!

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.310
If I find a Nasshi,
I’m totally catching it!

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:35.290
I know!

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.640
Any other regional variants, too!

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.790
I know that, too!

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:42.070
They make a pretty good team.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:43.840
Yeah.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.740
Isn’t it beautiful?

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.060
Yeah.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.350
Nothing beats the sea of Alola.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:13.770
It’s a Namakobushi!

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.830
Namakobushi! Sea Cucumber Pokémon!
Water type!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.080
It lives in shallow seas,
such as areas near a beach!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:27.380
It can eject its internal organs,
which it uses to engulf its prey or battle enemies!

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.960
Monster Ball, go!

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.090
Nice!

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:43.020
Namakobushi’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:45.380
All right!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.820
Hold it, Agojimushi!

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.780
It’s gonna dig! Don’t lose it!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.480
This way!

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.410
Yeah!

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.440
Go! Pikachu and I
will corner it,

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.360
so you catch it
when it comes out!

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:15.570
Go?

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.930
Hold it!

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.690
I <i>will</i> catch you!

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:30.690
An Alolan Dugtrio?!
Where’d you come from?!

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.590
Hooked a real big shot!

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:55.720
Alola, Mr. Soaked.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:57.970
Alola...

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.100
Um, actually...

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:03.270
I appreciate the greeting,
but I’d be happier if you let me down...

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.350
Sorry.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.200
You really saved me.

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:11.000
I’m Suiren. You?

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:11.860
Go.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:16.240
Wait, are you Satoshi’s friend?!

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.620
Go!

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:26.800
Where’d he go?

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.950
Satoshi! Pikachu!

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.880
Satoshi!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.290
Rotom!

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.130
I really missed you-roto!

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.140
Same!

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:40.700
Have you been well-roto?

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:42.980
Of course!

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:47.060
But I’m surprised you knew
we were here, Rotom.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.510
Heh-roto!

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:51.730
Rotom, Pokédex Forme.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:56.150
A Rotom Index, optimized for Pokémon Index
functionality. It has no other functions.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:10:00.610
How rude-roto! I have recording
and voice changing features, too-roto!

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:02.530
I forgot!

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:05.880
Everyone’s waiting for you at the Pokémon School,
so I came to get you-roto!

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:09.580
But I lost my friend, Go...

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:13.150
Go is already at the Pokémon School
with the others-roto.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:13.840
Huh?!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.090
It seems he ran into
Suiren at the sea-roto.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:19.380
I see! Suiren, huh?

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:35.150
So, what kind of foods
from Kanto do you like?

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:36.400
Um... I don’t know...

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:39.370
Say, is that a new kind of
Index Rotom?

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:40.960
This is a Smartphone Ro—

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:43.480
Smartphone?!
So you can make calls with it, too?!

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:44.050
Yeah...

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:46.480
Messon’s so cute!

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.750
Yeah...

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:52.110
You know how Satoshi tends
to run off on his own, right?

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:53.190
Has he caused any trouble?

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:54.830
Uh... I’m not sure...

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:57.900
Say, do you think I could dissect
your Smartphone Rotom?

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:59.570
D-Dissect?!

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:04.190
Please hurry up
and get here, Satoshi!

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:05.420
Alola!

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.700
<i>Alola!</i>

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:14.550
So you’re Go.

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:16.030
Yes, I am...?

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:19.030
I’m Kaki. Satoshi’s rival!

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.530
Rival?

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:21.910
Yeah.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.020
I was his rival while
he was in Alola, still am,

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:29.160
and will always be!

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:35.250
So who’s the stronger
battler of you?

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.620
You’re with Satoshi all the time,
aren’t you?

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:41.000
So you battle, too, don’t you?

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.010
Well... Every now and then.

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:46.810
“E-Every now and then”?!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.660
Hey, Kaki!

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:51.530
I cannot let that one slide!

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.810
Who are your Pokémon?

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.690
Those two?

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:04.410
I look forward to seeing
how well you have trained them.

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:13.130
Pocket Monsters!

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:21.470
Ground
Steel
Dugtrio

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.520
We’re back-roto!

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:34.520
Alola!

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.110
Guys!

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.110
<i>Satoshi!</i>

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:41.330
<i>Welcome back, Satoshi!</i>

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:42.340
It’s good to be back.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:44.450
Satoshi, what took you so long?!

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:46.530
I’m glad you’re okay, Go.

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:51.040
Everyone’s here now,
so let’s start the welcome party!

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.910
Agreed!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.670
<i>Cheers!</i>

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.920
Delicious!
What’s this juice?

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:01.920
It’s Aina Cafeteria’s special
Pile Juice!

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:08.820
You have to use fresh Pile Berries
and honey from Alola to get this taste.

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.180
I see.

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:15.550
Rabbifoot and Messon
seem to be really hungry, too.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:22.550
Mao’s dream is to make
people and Pokémon smile with her food.

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:25.160
That dream’s already a reality!

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.260
Thank you!

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:27.610
Mao’s the best!

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:30.950
Māmane, you’re gonna visit
Tokusane City again, right?

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:35.520
Yeah! I’m going to a workshop to research
the connection between Pokémon and space!

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:37.490
You’re really working hard, too!

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:39.590
W-Well... Yeah...

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.750
Māmane’s dream is
to become an astronaut-roto!

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.040
Really? That’s so cool!

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.470
Alola Surprise!

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.850
I just got this today!
It’s a letter from Lilie!

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.320
From Lilie?!

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:55.940
Who’s Lilie?

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.480
One of my friends
from the School.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.650
She’s on a journey
to find her father!

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:02.610
Ahem...

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:04.970
“Are all of you doing well?

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:11.930
“I, my brother and my mother
are all doing well.

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:18.580
Where is Mother?

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:22.690
She’s sending the data we got
last night to Aether Paradise.

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:23.960
The data from Magearna?

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:27.230
Yeah. She was really excited,
saying the more data we gather,

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:29.970
the more accurately
we can pinpoint his location.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:34.220
I have also started to feel...

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.890
...that we are getting
ever closer to Father.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:37.980
I see.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:51.890
“I wish to return to Alola...

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:54.090
“...together with Father.

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:56.910
“And then I would
very much like to see you all.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:58.380
“Suiren.

00:14:58.380 --> 00:14:59.690
“Māmane.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:00.940
“Kaki.

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:02.100
“Mao.

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:03.140
“Satoshi.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:07.800
“I will write to you again.
Signed, Lilie.”

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:10.670
All right!

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:15.710
Lilie’s giving it all she’s got!
We’d better do the same!

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:19.930
Hey, Kaki! It’s been a while,
so let’s battle!

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:21.820
A battle, huh? Sounds great!

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:23.070
Then it’s on!

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.440
But I...

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.190
...will battle <i>Go!</i>

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.690
Me?!

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:32.320
I will see if Go is worthy
of being Satoshi’s rival!

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.200
“Satoshi’s rival”...?

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:37.900
The person closest to Satoshi...

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:42.220
...needs to be strong enough
to be able to help him out with his dream!

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:45.670
H-Hey, Kaki,
you’re getting too fired up...

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.410
I agree with Mao.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:50.260
You gotta stay cool.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:52.240
Come on, Go!

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:53.830
Wait, Kaki!

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:54.780
All right.

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:55.650
Huh?!

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.180
How can I refuse
after hearing all of that?

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:00.390
Go...

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:04.870
I’ve got my own pride to protect.

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:05.650
Yeah?

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.960
Bakugames! Dragon Tail!

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:28.550
Dodge it, Rabbifoot!

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:31.050
Then use Double Kick!

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:41.300
Good, Rabbifoot!

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:43.890
You’re not bad!

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.350
Of course!

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.030
That’s it.

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:50.990
I will use my Z-Move!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:59.990
Z-Moves are the strongest moves in Alola, born by
unleashing the full power of both trainer and Pokémon!

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:02.000
The strongest in Alola...

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:04.350
If you want to run, do it now.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:06.100
There’s no way I’d run!

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:08.630
Just as I would expect
from Satoshi’s rival.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.890
You keep calling me his rival...

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.880
You are wrong!

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:15.880
What?

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.510
I’m not Satoshi’s rival.

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:24.140
And I have no intention
of helping Satoshi reach his dream.

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:29.400
Dreams are something you reach
with your <i>own</i> power, yeah?

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:31.130
My dream...

00:17:31.930 --> 00:17:34.740
My <i>future</i> lies in my hands!

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:36.530
Satoshi feels the same way.

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:39.790
Use your Z-Move.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.000
I’m no rival,

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:47.390
but I am Satoshi’s
research fellow partner... His friend!

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:52.920
And as his friend, I want to show him
a battle I can be proud of!

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.680
I like your courage.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:18:00.260
Here we go, Bakugames!

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:04.730
My full body...

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.110
...soul...

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:07.520
...and power!

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.310
The zenith of all that I am...

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:13.730
Become a blazing flame that burns
like the mountain of Akala!

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:20.740
Rabbifoot, let’s put all the power
we can muster into this attack!

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:26.460
Dynamic Full Flame!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:34.590
Go! Ember!

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:43.560
Go!

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.420
Why are we...?

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:01.290
Garagara?!

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.220
Go and Rabbifoot are there, too.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:05.400
Garagara saved them.

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:09.160
I’m sure this was Kaki’s plan
from the beginning.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:09.830
<i>Huh?</i>

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:15.350
Well done, Garagara.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:22.420
Go.

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:23.550
What?

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:25.590
Look after Satoshi for me.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:32.560
Kaki...

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:39.780
I may not be his rival,
but I can certainly look after him for you!

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:44.410
You really are stubborn.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.860
This coming from <i>you?</i>

00:19:57.430 --> 00:19:58.860
Say, Go...

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:01.090
What is your dream?

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:03.260
My dream is...

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:08.590
...to catch every Pokémon,
to work my way up to Mew!

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:13.050
Um, the applause is a bit...

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:15.110
...embarrassing...

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.600
You gotta catch it!

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:22.860
<i>You can do it!</i>

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:26.950
Use Ember, Rabbifoot!

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:32.560
Good!

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:33.750
Now, do it!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.400
Monster Ball, go!

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:45.340
All right!

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.220
You did it, Go!

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:53.070
Nasshi: Alolan Form’s data
will be added to the Index!

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:54.730
Nasshi! Coconut Pokémon!

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:57.200
Leave the rest to me-roto!

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.230
Grass/Dragon type.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:02.120
Alola is the best environment
for this Pokémon.

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:08.220
Local people take pride in its appearance,
saying this is how Nasshi ought to look.

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:13.290
Come out!

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:21.190
Two kinds of Nasshi...
That’s great!

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:22.170
Yeah.

00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:24.310
Hey, Satoshi.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.850
Let’s go to Alola again sometime.

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:29.920
Yeah! That’s a promise!

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:34.930
Satoshi and Go have had fun
with their friends in Alola.

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:41.530
What region will their
next adventure be set in?

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:51.720
Mew!

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:52.470
Warrgle!

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:53.260
